WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.210
In 1819, the poet John
Keats wrote a letter.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.430
Call the world, he wrote,
the vale of soul-making.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.820
Long before, Irenaeus taught that
humans were created like children:

4
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.620
not perfect, but able to grow.

5
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:20.110
So would a world with no pain at
all be a better place to grow up in?

6
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.700
In this mission, you'll test
John Hick's thought experiment:

7
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.720
a world where God prevents every harm.

8
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:32.190
Then you'll face the hardest cases:
suffering that crushes rather than builds.

9
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.670
Your mission: weigh up whether a world
with no pain would be a better place to

10
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.330
grow.
